1
00:00:00,330 --> 00:00:02,960
宇宙大爆炸
The Big Bang.

2
00:00:05,110 --> 00:00:06,910
...能量洪流
...A torrent of energy

3
00:00:06,910 --> 00:00:11,410
将我们的宇宙从一无所有 转换为多姿多彩
that propelled our Universe from nothing into everything,

4
00:00:11,410 --> 00:00:14,820
创造了空间和时间
creating both space and time.

5
00:00:15,950 --> 00:00:17,420
截至目前，这是关于
It's the best theory yet

6
00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:19,950
时间之始的最好理论
of what happened at the beginning of time.

7
00:00:21,690 --> 00:00:23,320
但是，新一代的科学家们
But a new generation of scientists

8
00:00:23,330 --> 00:00:27,760
敢于深思曾被认为 不可能的问题——
is daring to contemplate what was once thought impossible --

9
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:30,160
宇宙大爆炸理论存在错误吗？
are we wrong about the Big Bang?

10
00:00:30,970 --> 00:00:35,800
也许我们很快就能发现 在宇宙太初究竟发生了什么
And might we soon discover what happened before the beginning?

11
00:00:40,910 --> 00:00:46,010
空间，时间，生命本身
Space, time, life itself.

12
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:52,350
宇宙的秘密，尽在穿越虫洞
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

13
00:00:52,390 --> 00:00:55,720
♪穿越虫洞，第1x04集♪
♪Through the Wormhole 1x04♪

14
00:00:56,020 --> 00:00:59,990
太初之前，宇宙若何？
What Happened Before the Beginning?

15
00:01:00,730 --> 00:01:04,000
宇宙是如何开始的？
How did the Universe begin?

16
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,030
我们都曾耳闻大爆炸
We've all heard of the Big Bang,

17
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:09,140
但是我们究竟如何证明 这个理论的正确性？
but how do we really know that's the way it was?

18
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:12,570
我的意思是，毕竟当时没有目击者
I mean, after all, nobody was around to see it happen.

19
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:18,050
如果这个问题不好回答，试试这个——
And if that question seems hard to answer, try this one --

20
00:01:18,050 --> 00:01:22,650
在宇宙开始之前 发生了什么？
what happened before the Universe began?

21
00:01:22,650 --> 00:01:23,850
[铃儿叮当]
[ Bell clangs ]

22
00:01:23,850 --> 00:01:26,890
我第一次遭遇 这个永恒的问题
I first encountered this eternal question

23
00:01:26,890 --> 00:01:28,620
是在卫理公会教堂里
at the Methodist church.

24
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:31,260
♪歌词：美好的车子♪ 
Sweet chariot

25
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:34,460
♪歌词：前来接我回家♪ 
coming for to carry me home

26
00:01:34,460 --> 00:01:36,870
弗里曼：在《创世纪》中，上帝说
(Freeman) In the book of Genesis, God said,

27
00:01:36,870 --> 00:01:40,840
"要有光，于是有了光"
"let there be light, and there was light."

28
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:45,270
上帝创造了天和地
God then created the Heavens and the Earth.

29
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:50,280
但是，如果万物皆由此始
But if everything began at this moment,

30
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:53,150
上帝当时身处何样世界呢？
how was God around to create it?

31
00:01:55,750 --> 00:01:59,820
在时间开始之前，另有时间吗？
Could there ever have been a time before time?

32
00:01:59,820 --> 00:02:02,060
[蟋蟀声声]
[ Crickets chirping ]

33
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:03,790
这是个问题
It's a question

34
00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:07,000
5000多年来，不断的激发 科学家，哲学家
that has intrigued scientists and philosophers

35
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:11,330
以及我们这些普罗大众 的好奇心
and the rest of us for more than 5,000 years.

36
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:16,140
但在1920年代， 一个科学家发现了
But in the 1920s, a scientific discovery

37
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:19,240
时间开始那一刻 宇宙中闪耀的别样光线
shone some new light on the beginning of time

38
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:22,540
以及创世前的可能景象
and what might have come before,

39
00:02:22,550 --> 00:02:26,250
感谢这个人——Edwin Hubble
thanks to this man -- Edwin Hubble.

40
00:02:26,250 --> 00:02:29,280
在南加州的Wilson山顶上
Atop Mount Wilson in Southern California,

41
00:02:29,290 --> 00:02:33,020
Hubble架起了一个 瞄准天堂的新型大杀器
Hubble aimed a powerful, new weapon at the heavens --

42
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:37,090
强大的Hook 101英寸望远镜
the mighty Hooker 101-inch telescope.

43
00:02:37,090 --> 00:02:39,630
他通过望远镜嘹望宇宙
As he looked through it,

44
00:02:39,630 --> 00:02:42,130
成为第一个鉴赏
he became the first man to appreciate

45
00:02:42,130 --> 00:02:44,070
宇宙真实格局的人
the true scale of the Universe.

46
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:49,200
Hubble 看到，天空中的 模糊小斑点
Hubble saw that small patches of blurry sky

47
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:53,680
并不是气体星云， 实际上是其他的星系
were not gas clusters, but in fact other galaxies.

48
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:57,680
宇宙中的星系，不是几千个
The Universe was filled with not thousands,

49
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:00,920
而是有几百亿个
but hundreds of billions of them.

50
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:05,890
Hubble的观察 还有更具意义的发现
Remarkable as this discovery was, Hubble's observations

51
00:03:05,890 --> 00:03:10,390
观察到的现象推导出一个 影响深远的结论——
would lead to an even more profound conclusion --

52
00:03:10,390 --> 00:03:14,230
宇宙在膨胀
the Universe is expanding,

53
00:03:14,230 --> 00:03:20,040
每个星系都在越来越快的 彼此远离
every single galaxy drifting farther and farther apart.

54
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:22,270
如果反向推导
Run this picture back in time,

55
00:03:22,270 --> 00:03:25,510
所有的数学推理 都指向一个时刻
and all the math points to a single moment

56
00:03:25,510 --> 00:03:29,240
那时，我们的宇宙是一个 体积无穷小，密度无穷大的
of an infinitely small, infinitely dense beginning

57
00:03:29,250 --> 00:03:31,410
起始点
to our Universe.

58
00:03:31,410 --> 00:03:36,020
科学家为这一初始状态 起了个名字——奇点
Scientists have a name for this initial state -- a singularity.

59
00:03:37,350 --> 00:03:42,890
在大爆炸之前， 没有空间，没有时间
Before this Big Bang, there is nowhere and no-when.

60
00:03:42,890 --> 00:03:47,000
在宇宙开始前， 真正的一无所有
There is literally nothing before this beginning.

61
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,400
从奇点开始计时
Run the clock forward from that singularity,

62
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:53,500
发令枪就是大爆炸
and the starting gun is the Big Bang...

63
00:03:58,070 --> 00:04:01,740
...一次能量和物质的巨大爆炸
...A colossal explosion of energy and matter

64
00:04:01,740 --> 00:04:06,080
天空中目之所及的万物 都是自此开始
that gave birth to everything we see in the sky today.

65
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:10,490
大爆炸还创造了空间和时间
It also created space and time.

66
00:04:10,490 --> 00:04:12,690
所有的辐射和物质射出
As all the radiation and matter

67
00:04:12,690 --> 00:04:15,390
射向四面八方
shoots out in different directions,

68
00:04:15,390 --> 00:04:18,290
然后宇宙终于开始冷却
the Universe eventually starts to cool.

69
00:04:18,290 --> 00:04:21,230
引力导致物质聚集
Gravity causes matter to clump together,

70
00:04:21,230 --> 00:04:23,930
恒星孕育...
and stars are born...

71
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:26,870
然后又爆发
And then explode.

72
00:04:34,410 --> 00:04:38,110
接下来，灰尘和岩石 如同旋转的碟子
Later, swirling discs of dust and rocks

73
00:04:38,110 --> 00:04:40,950
围绕着新生的恒星
gather around newer stars.

74
00:04:44,090 --> 00:04:48,590
实际上，在大爆炸之后 几十亿年
Eventually, several billion years after the Big Bang,

75
00:04:48,590 --> 00:04:53,100
像地球这样的行星才诞生
we get a planet like Earth.

76
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:57,470
这个令人头疼的故事 已经变成了经典
This mind-twisting story has become the new dogma,

77
00:04:57,470 --> 00:04:59,470
坚定有力
but however robust,

78
00:04:59,470 --> 00:05:03,240
大爆炸仍然只是一个理论
the Big Bang is still just a theory.

79
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:06,510
普林斯顿的物理学教授 David Spergel博士
Princeton Professor of physics Dr. David Spergel

80
00:05:06,510 --> 00:05:08,410
将大部分研究精力投入到
has spent much of his career

81
00:05:08,410 --> 00:05:12,680
研究这场宇宙巨变 是否以及怎样发生的
trying to understand if and how this cataclysmic event happened.

82
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:16,450
人们常常叫他 "宇宙先生"
People sometimes call him "Mr. Universe."

83
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:21,360
对Spergel来说，大爆炸
For Spergel, the Big Bang

84
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:24,760
仍然是关于早期宇宙的
is still the most complete and scientifically sound model

85
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:26,160
最完备和最科学的模型
of the early Universe.

86
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:30,400
我们身边的万事万物 来自于大爆炸
Everything around us came from the hot Big Bang.

87
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:33,600
宇宙起始—— 大爆炸理论
The Universe started out -- Big Bang Theory --

88
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:35,470
非常非常热，密度非常大
very, very hot, very dense.

89
00:05:35,470 --> 00:05:37,940
热辐射冷却了
That hot radiation cooled.

90
00:05:37,940 --> 00:05:42,140
那些物质、辐射能量
From that emerged matter, radiation,

91
00:05:42,150 --> 00:05:44,110
最终构成了我们身边的世界
everything that makes up the world around us.

92
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:49,620
现在，我们在位于Crawford山的 贝尔实验室
And here we are at Bell Labs at Crawford Hill,

93
00:05:49,620 --> 00:05:52,650
从某种意义上讲 当红的大爆炸理论
the place where the hot Big Bang theory really all started,

94
00:05:52,660 --> 00:05:54,160
始于此处
in some ways.

95
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:57,960
Arno Penzias和Robert Wilson 是一对射电天文学家
Arno Penzias and Robert Wilson are a pair of radio astronomers

96
00:05:57,960 --> 00:06:00,430
在这里，为贝尔实验室工作
who worked here at Bell Laboratories.

97
00:06:00,430 --> 00:06:04,570
他们的工作是 研究天空中的微波
What they were doing is they were studying the microwave sky

98
00:06:04,570 --> 00:06:05,900
贝尔实验室试图利用
as Bell Labs was exploring

99
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:08,370
这些微波进行通讯
the idea of using it for microwave communication.

100
00:06:08,370 --> 00:06:11,010
弗里曼：那是在1964年
(Freeman) It was 1964.

101
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:14,180
那时候
At this point,

102
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:17,250
这两个人没想过要解决什么 宇宙的大问题
the two men were not trying to solve any big cosmic questions.

103
00:06:17,250 --> 00:06:20,280
他们在处理工作中的鬼事情
They were just trying to get the darn thing to work.

104
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:21,650
[ 嘶嘶声 ]
[ Hissing ]

105
00:06:21,650 --> 00:06:23,950
对初学者来说 神秘的嘶嘶声
For starters, a mysterious hiss

106
00:06:23,950 --> 00:06:26,420
是对无线信号的干扰
was interfering with their radio signal.

107
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:30,090
Spergel博士:Penzias和Wilson 是非常优秀的射电天文学家
Dr. Spergel: Penzias and Wilson were really good radio astronomers,

108
00:06:30,090 --> 00:06:32,160
他们建造了一个很棒的望远镜
so they built a really nice telescope.

109
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:35,000
他们的设计是， 即使有背景噪声
And they designed it so there shouldn't be any background,

110
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,060
也不会造成影响
yet it was there.

111
00:06:36,070 --> 00:06:38,470
弗里曼：他们听到的背景噪声
(Freeman) This background hiss they heard

112
00:06:38,470 --> 00:06:40,500
来自天空中的各个方向
was coming from every corner of the sky.

113
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:43,470
Wilson和Penzias尝试了各种手段
Wilson and Penzias tried everything,

114
00:06:43,470 --> 00:06:47,480
甚至包括打扫掉天线上的 灰尘和落叶
even sweeping the dirt and leaves out of the antenna,

115
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:49,480
噪声依旧
but still there was noise.

116
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:52,080
他们尝试用液氦 冷却接收器
They tried cooling the receivers with liquid helium.

117
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:54,750
噪声依旧
Still there was noise.

118
00:06:54,750 --> 00:06:57,790
他们甚至给一窝鸽子搬了家
They even removed a family of nesting pigeons

119
00:06:57,790 --> 00:06:59,960
清理了鸽子留下的纪念品
and their associated droppings.

120
00:06:59,960 --> 00:07:02,890
但是，噪声不想走
And still the noise would not go away.

121
00:07:02,890 --> 00:07:06,760
有时，科学研究就是将 多余因素排除掉
Sometimes science consists of cleaning up a lot of stuff

122
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:08,830
看看究竟剩下什么
and seeing what's left behind.

123
00:07:08,830 --> 00:07:11,600
在排除了他们所能想到的 一切因素之后
Having eliminated anything they can think of,

124
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:14,670
他们意识到 是有别的什么东西存在
they realized there had to be something else there.

125
00:07:14,670 --> 00:07:17,570
唯一的可能性就是
Penzias: Penzias: The only possibility

126
00:07:17,570 --> 00:07:20,280
噪声来自于我们星系 之外的什么地方
was that it was coming from someplace outside our galaxy,

127
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:22,310
这听上去是个如此奇特的想法
and that seemed like such a far-out idea.

128
00:07:22,310 --> 00:07:25,810
我们不知道要做什么
We just didn't know what to do with that result.

129
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:29,080
弗里曼：在咨询了普利斯顿的 物理学家们之后
(Freeman) Consulting with a team of Princeton physicists,

130
00:07:29,090 --> 00:07:31,950
Wilson和Penzias意识到 能从天空中各个角落
Wilson and Penzias realized that the only reason

131
00:07:31,950 --> 00:07:34,760
接收到信号的唯一原因是
something could come from every part of the sky

132
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:40,230
这个信号是某种巨大的 宇宙事件的微弱回声
is if it were actually a faint echo of a huge cosmic event.

133
00:07:40,230 --> 00:07:43,700
我们测量了背景温度
We had really measured the background temperature,

134
00:07:43,700 --> 00:07:46,870
这种残余噪声是来自 宇宙的创始
the remnant noise from the creation of the Universe.

135
00:07:46,870 --> 00:07:50,210
弗里曼：全世界一些最著名的科学家
(Freeman) After 40 years of speculation and calculation

136
00:07:50,210 --> 00:07:53,410
进行了40年的思考和计算
by some of the most famous scientists in the world,

137
00:07:53,410 --> 00:07:56,710
证明了，这两个射电工程师 偶然接收到的
the two radio engineers had stumbled upon a faint cry

138
00:07:56,710 --> 00:07:58,880
是我们宇宙初生时的 微弱啼哭声
from our own cosmic birth.

139
00:07:58,880 --> 00:08:00,680
[ 嘶嘶声继续 ]
[ Hissing continues ]

140
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:03,180
产生这些嘶嘶声的原因是
The cause of the hiss had to be

141
00:08:03,190 --> 00:08:06,320
大爆炸残留的热量
the leftover heat from the Big Bang.

142
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:09,290
一幅时间和空间诞生的图像
A picture of the beginning of time and space

143
00:08:09,290 --> 00:08:12,190
开始渐渐成型了
was starting to emerge.

144
00:08:12,190 --> 00:08:15,230
Dr. Spergel：这个气球就是我们的整个宇宙
(Dr. Spergel)This balloon is our whole Universe.

145
00:08:15,230 --> 00:08:16,930
当我扩张这个宇宙...
As I expand the Universe...

146
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:21,740
...注意看，气球上的东西
...Notice how all the things on the balloon

147
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:23,100
是如何远离彼此的
move apart from each other.

148
00:08:23,110 --> 00:08:25,210
我们不是在宇宙的中心
We're not in the center of the Universe.

149
00:08:25,210 --> 00:08:28,240
整个宇宙都在膨胀——随着时间膨胀
It's the whole Universe that's expanding -- expanding in time.

150
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:29,680
对辐射来说，也是这样的
Same is true with the radiation.

151
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:32,180
并不是说微波冲我们飞来
It's not that the microwave radiation is coming towards us

152
00:08:32,180 --> 00:08:34,020
我们并不是在大爆炸的中心
and we're in the center of the Big Bang.

153
00:08:34,020 --> 00:08:38,090
整个气球都充满了 大爆炸产生的辐射
The whole balloon is filled with radiation from the Big Bang.

154
00:08:38,090 --> 00:08:41,090
当气球膨胀，辐射温度降低
As the balloon expands, the radiation gets colder.

155
00:08:41,090 --> 00:08:43,760
气球越大，宇宙的温度越低
Bigger the balloon, colder the Universe is.

156
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:46,260
我们现在反推时间
We can now run the Universe back in time.

157
00:08:46,260 --> 00:08:47,900
宇宙在收缩
The Universe is contracting,

158
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:51,370
越来越热，越来越热 越来越热，还在变热
getting hotter, getting hotter, getting hotter, hotter still.

159
00:08:51,370 --> 00:08:54,200
我们现在回到了初始奇点时刻
We're now back at the moment of initial singularity.

160
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:56,970
这就是大爆炸开始的时刻
We're at the moment in which the Big Bang started.

161
00:08:56,970 --> 00:08:59,940
所有的一切——所有的空间都压缩在这里
Everything -- all of space -- is contracted right here.

162
00:08:59,940 --> 00:09:02,280
这是炽热辐射产生的时刻
This is when the hot radiation was generated.

163
00:09:02,280 --> 00:09:06,080
并不是在一点产生 而是在各处产生
It's not generated in one spot. It's generated everywhere.

164
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:10,020
大爆炸在这个气球表面的 各点开始爆发
The Big Bang happened everywhere on the surface of the balloon.

165
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:12,250
弗里曼：宇宙背景辐射微波
(Freeman) The accidental discovery

166
00:09:12,250 --> 00:09:14,720
这一偶然发现
of cosmic microwave background radiation

167
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:18,530
