334
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:49,470
但，并不是所有人都信这一套
But not for everybody.

335
00:17:50,540 --> 00:17:54,380
以此解释宇宙诞生只不过是 一种精神上的寄托
Interpreting this as a beginning is indeed just a crutch.

336
00:17:54,380 --> 00:17:56,810
它没有任何理论根据
It's not derived from any theory.

337
00:17:56,810 --> 00:17:59,480
在奇点，所有的理论都失效了
It's just a place where the theory itself breaks down.

338
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:02,320
弗里曼：Martin Bojowald博士 物理学教授，供职于
(Freeman) Dr. Martin Bojowald is a Professor of Physics

339
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:06,620
宾州州立大学引力和宇宙学院
at the institute for Gravitation and the Cosmos at Penn State.

340
00:18:06,620 --> 00:18:10,760
他是新一代宇宙学家中 升起的新星
He's a rising star in a new generation of cosmologists

341
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:13,160
正在向长久以来奉为经典的
which is challenging some long-held beliefs

342
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:15,160
宇宙学说进行挑战
about the Universe.

343
00:18:15,170 --> 00:18:18,670
膨胀也许修饰了第二幕
Inflation may have fixed act two,

344
00:18:18,670 --> 00:18:20,040
但是Martin认为
but Martin thinks

345
00:18:20,040 --> 00:18:22,500
这个戏的第一幕太离谱
the play still starts with a very unlikely act one --

346
00:18:22,510 --> 00:18:26,240
奇点突然从一无所有
the sudden and singular pop

347
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:30,080
变成了整个宇宙
from nothing into the entire Universe.

348
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:31,310
所谓的奇点只是说明
A singularity just means

349
00:18:31,310 --> 00:18:33,680
我们对理论理解的远远不够
we don't understand the theory well enough.

350
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:36,820
弗里曼：Alan Guth用膨胀的理论
(Freeman) Alan Guth used the theory of inflation

351
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:40,660
深入研究在宇宙开始 万亿万亿万亿分之一秒后
to dig down to a trillion, trillion, trillionth of a second

352
00:18:40,660 --> 00:18:41,990
的真实情况
after the beginning.

353
00:18:42,930 --> 00:18:46,860
Martin更近了一百万倍
Martin went a million times closer.

354
00:18:46,860 --> 00:18:50,630
在Bojowald的理论中， 时间并不是自由流转的
In Bojowald's theory, time is not free-flowing,

355
00:18:50,630 --> 00:18:54,540
而是由离散的 可以测量的小块组成
but made up of discrete, measurable chunks.

356
00:18:54,540 --> 00:18:58,470
这些时间的小块被称为 "时空原子"
These chunks of time are called "space-time atoms."

357
00:18:58,470 --> 00:19:00,180
这是研究宇宙创世前情景的
It's a very different way

358
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:03,680
全新思路
of thinking about what happened before the beginning.

359
00:19:03,680 --> 00:19:06,550
[ 钟表滴答 ]
[ Clock ticking ]

360
00:19:06,550 --> 00:19:09,920
Bojowald博士：这里，我们有一个 漂亮的，老祖父级的表
(Dr. Bojowald) Here we have a beautiful, old grandfather clock.

361
00:19:09,920 --> 00:19:12,390
如我们所见， 有一个钟摆
As we can see, there's a pendulum.

362
00:19:12,390 --> 00:19:14,890
它以连续的方式摇摆
It's swinging in a continuous way,

363
00:19:14,890 --> 00:19:17,830
告诉钟时间如何流逝
thereby telling the clock how time is proceeding.

364
00:19:17,830 --> 00:19:19,460
并没有离散的记号
They're not discrete marks,

365
00:19:19,460 --> 00:19:24,030
只有钟摆的连续运动
but rather a continuous motion of the pendulum.

366
00:19:24,030 --> 00:19:29,040
这是时间连续测量的 经典画面
This is the classical picture of time measured continuously.

367
00:19:29,040 --> 00:19:32,940
现在，量子化的时间 这可是完全不同的故事
Now, in quantized time, it's a whole different story.

368
00:19:32,940 --> 00:19:35,980
对于量子化的时间， 我们有这样的情形
For quantized time, we have a picture

369
00:19:35,980 --> 00:19:38,650
由秒针指明时间
as given by the second hand of the clock here.

370
00:19:38,650 --> 00:19:39,880
时间并不连续
It's not continuous.

371
00:19:39,880 --> 00:19:41,480
时间并不是钟摆
It's not the pendulum swing,

372
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:45,120
那个我们可以随时随地 停止的钟摆
which we could stop at any time, at any position.

373
00:19:45,120 --> 00:19:47,420
在这儿，某个离散集合给定了
Here, the different positions are given

374
00:19:47,420 --> 00:19:51,760
计时点之间的不同位置
by certain discrete sets between one tick and the next one.

375
00:19:51,760 --> 00:19:53,860
有限数量的时间
It's a finite amount of time

376
00:19:53,860 --> 00:19:55,960
不可再分的时间单位
which cannot be further subdivided.

377
00:19:55,970 --> 00:19:59,330
弗里曼：在Bojowald版本的 早期宇宙中
(Freeman) In Bojowald's version of the early Universe,

378
00:19:59,340 --> 00:20:00,900
你不会遭遇虚无
you never get to nothing.

379
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:03,370
量子化时钟的秒针
The second hand on the quantized clock

380
00:20:03,370 --> 00:20:06,070
并不只标记一个时刻的开始
marks not just the beginning of one moment,

381
00:20:06,080 --> 00:20:07,910
还是另一个时刻的结束
but the end of another.

382
00:20:07,910 --> 00:20:11,750
在我们宇宙黎明结束 的那一声滴答
The tick that signaled dawn in our Universe

383
00:20:11,750 --> 00:20:15,250
也标记了午夜的结束
marks one second past midnight in the last.

384
00:20:15,250 --> 00:20:16,750
[ 时钟滴答 ]
[ Clock ticking ]

385
00:20:16,750 --> 00:20:20,590
Dr. Bojowald：因此 我们有了这个宇宙气球
(Dr. Bojowald) So, we have this balloon Universe.

386
00:20:20,590 --> 00:20:23,890
如果我们假象 在大爆炸之前的情形
If we imagine what it could have been before the Big Bang,

387
00:20:23,890 --> 00:20:27,830
它在崩毁 所以体积在收缩
it was collapsing, so the volume was shrinking.

388
00:20:27,830 --> 00:20:30,300
现在，如果我们 按照通常的演化观
Now, if we follow the usual evolution,

389
00:20:30,300 --> 00:20:32,230
根据广义相对论
according to general relativity,

390
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:35,070
收缩会以奇点结束
that would have been ending in a singularity.

391
00:20:35,070 --> 00:20:38,070
整个气球完全的收缩了
The whole balloon would just completely deflate.

392
00:20:38,070 --> 00:20:41,640
但是按照空间和时间 的原子性
But with the atomic nature of space and time,

393
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:44,750
引力的吸引性改变了
the attractive behavior of gravity changes.

394
00:20:44,750 --> 00:20:47,720
在如此高的密度下 引力变成了斥力
It becomes repulsive at these high densities.

395
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:49,120
崩塌停止了
The collapse stops.

396
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:52,550
力反了过来 有了斥力
Then the forces turn around, so there's a repulsive force

397
00:20:52,560 --> 00:20:54,820
使宇宙再次膨胀
which makes the Universe re-expand.

398
00:20:56,730 --> 00:20:59,530
在某个时刻— 我们还不太确定—
At some point -- we're not sure yet --

399
00:20:59,530 --> 00:21:03,130
但宇宙可能在未来某个时刻 再次崩塌
but it might recollapse at some time in the future,

400
00:21:03,130 --> 00:21:06,440
所有的气体可能再次跑掉
so all the air might go out again.

401
00:21:06,440 --> 00:21:08,400
体积会收缩
The volume would decrease,

402
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:10,410
密度增加
the density would increase,

403
00:21:10,410 --> 00:21:13,780
然后接近另一次大爆炸
and then probably approach another Big Bang.

404
00:21:13,780 --> 00:21:17,580
弗里曼：宇宙膨胀又收缩
(Freeman) The Universe expands and contracts,

405
00:21:17,580 --> 00:21:20,620
但它从未有真正的起点
but it never actually begins.

406
00:21:20,620 --> 00:21:23,950
在当前这个宇宙之前 也许有一系列的宇宙
There could have been a series of Universes before this one

407
00:21:23,950 --> 00:21:27,320
其后，将有更多的继任
and more to come after this one.

408
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:31,630
Bojowald正在研究这些问题
Bojowald is working through the problems and conundrums

409
00:21:31,630 --> 00:21:34,600
创立了全新的理论学说
that all radical new theories face.

410
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:38,970
他的理论并不完备 也许永远不会完备
His theory is by no means complete, and it may never be.

411
00:21:40,100 --> 00:21:42,340
Bojowald博士：我们还在 研究等式
(Dr. Bojowald) We are still working on the equations.

412
00:21:42,340 --> 00:21:44,040
我们还没有完备的答案
We don't have the complete answer yet,

413
00:21:44,040 --> 00:21:45,770
但这看上去是解决这个问题的
but it seems to be the best theory yet

414
00:21:45,780 --> 00:21:47,380
最好理论
to address these issues.

415
00:21:48,850 --> 00:21:50,510
[ 钟声，时钟滴答 ]
[ Bell tolls, clock ticking ]

416
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:54,480
弗里曼：但在2001年
(Freeman) But in 2001,

417
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:57,390
世界上两个顶尖的宇宙学家
two of the leading cosmologists in the world

418
00:21:57,390 --> 00:22:00,490
发表了一篇论文 对关于宇宙形成问题
published a paper suggesting an even more radical approach

419
00:22:00,490 --> 00:22:02,620
提出了更激进的假说
to what happened at the beginning.

420
00:22:02,630 --> 00:22:04,630
这两个宇宙学家的观点认为
For these two scientists,

421
00:22:04,630 --> 00:22:07,660
有另一种答案，如此的 怪异和超出想象
there was another answer so strange and unexpected

422
00:22:07,660 --> 00:22:10,170
以至于从未有人考虑过
that it had never been considered.

423
00:22:10,170 --> 00:22:13,370
一直都存在着爆炸、爆炸、爆炸
There are bangs and bangs and bangs forever.

424
00:22:13,370 --> 00:22:16,670
弗里曼：我们的宇宙 也许不是唯一的一个
(Freeman) Our Universe may not be the only one,

425
00:22:16,670 --> 00:22:21,480
也许只是几百个、几千个 甚至无数个宇宙之一
but one of hundreds, thousands, maybe an infinite number.

426
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:24,910
这是个让人感兴趣却又 令人气馁的假设——
It's an inspiring and daunting suggestion --

427
00:22:24,910 --> 00:22:27,320
宇宙是由一系列的爆炸驱动的
the Universe is an endless cycle

428
00:22:27,320 --> 00:22:31,020
无尽的循环
prompted by an endless series of bangs,

429
00:22:31,020 --> 00:22:32,850
永远持续
forever.

430
00:22:37,290 --> 00:22:39,690
弗里曼：当你遥望星空
(Freeman) When you look out into space,

431
00:22:39,690 --> 00:22:42,090
注目一个遥远的星星
gaze at a distant star,

432
00:22:42,090 --> 00:22:44,830
你也在回望过去
you also look back in time.

433
00:22:44,830 --> 00:22:46,730
遥远行星飞来的光线
Light from distant galaxies

434
00:22:46,730 --> 00:22:49,570
需要旅行几十亿年 才到达我们这里
can take billions of years to reach us.

435
00:22:49,570 --> 00:22:53,340
现在，我们知道，存在一个界限 我们回望过去却不能超过界限
Now we know there's a limit to how far back we can see,

436
00:22:53,340 --> 00:22:55,540
一个可见宇宙的边界
an edge to the visible Universe.

437
00:22:55,540 --> 00:22:57,910
从过去宇宙飞来的光
The light from that cosmic backdrop

438
00:22:57,910 --> 00:23:03,450
到达地球前已经飞行了137亿年
has taken 13.7 billion years to make it to Earth.

439
00:23:03,450 --> 00:23:07,020
在幕后隐藏着什么？
What lies beyond that curtain?

440
00:23:07,020 --> 00:23:09,920
按照Martin Bojowald教授的说法
According to Professor Martin Bojowald,

441
00:23:09,920 --> 00:23:12,590
时间在奇点附近
time becomes squeezed and distorted

442
00:23:12,590 --> 00:23:14,430
挤压扭曲
as it nears a singularity

443
00:23:14,430 --> 00:23:18,760
反弹回来，进入另一个扩展过程
and then bounces back out into another expansion.

444
00:23:18,760 --> 00:23:22,270
但是也许存在 另一个完全不同的方式
But perhaps there's an altogether different way

445
00:23:22,270 --> 00:23:25,740
能够回看宇宙创世的情景
to look at what happened before the beginning.

446
00:23:27,630 --> 00:23:30,760
南非科学家Neil Turok博士
South African scientist Dr. Neil Turok

447
00:23:30,770 --> 00:23:32,630
现在敢于比大多数的其他人
is now daring to go further into the past

448
00:23:32,630 --> 00:23:34,530
更进一步
than almost anyone else.

449
00:23:34,630 --> 00:23:38,930
弗里曼：从他开始从事 理论物理的研究
(Freeman) From the moment he entered the field of theoretical physics,

450
00:23:38,930 --> 00:23:40,600
这个南非科学家
the South African scientist

451
00:23:40,600 --> 00:23:44,200
就致力于 为这个老问题寻找新答案
was looking for new answers to age-old problems.

452
00:23:44,200 --> 00:23:47,340
Turok博士：人们总习惯于
(Dr. Turok) There is a conventional wisdom

453
00:23:47,340 --> 00:23:48,470
墨守成规
in the field,

454
00:23:48,480 --> 00:23:51,810
对新想法接受很慢
and people are very slow to adopt new ideas.

455
00:23:51,810 --> 00:23:53,110
而且，坦白说
And, frankly,

456
00:23:53,110 --> 00:23:56,620
许多人的职业生涯 安于现状
many people have built their careers on the status quo,

457
00:23:56,620 --> 00:23:58,620
他们不想要新想法
and they don't want a new idea

458
00:23:58,620 --> 00:24:01,050
制造麻烦
coming along and rocking the boat.

459
00:24:01,050 --> 00:24:03,890
弗里曼：与其他同事不同，
(Freeman) For Neil, the WMAP announcement

460
00:24:03,890 --> 00:24:06,730
Neil觉得WMAP的发现 和他通过不同的望远镜
brought up familiar feelings about seeing the Universe

461
00:24:06,730 --> 00:24:08,530
观察宇宙的感觉
through a slightly different lens

462
00:24:08,530 --> 00:24:10,830
很相似
than some of his colleagues.

463
00:24:10,830 --> 00:24:13,130
Turok博士：在WMAP的新闻发布会上
(Dr. Turok) In the WMAP press announcement,

464
00:24:13,130 --> 00:24:15,330
当然，参与的科学家们
of course the scientists involved

465
00:24:15,340 --> 00:24:17,500
将它与膨胀明确的联系起来
linked it explicitly to inflation

466
00:24:17,500 --> 00:24:20,540
并说，"戏剧性的证实了膨胀现象"
and said, "this dramatically confirms inflation."

467
00:24:20,540 --> 00:24:23,310
这令我坐立不安 [笑]
And this made me squirm. [ laughs ]

468
00:24:23,310 --> 00:24:24,940
我的观点是
My point of view

469
00:24:24,950 --> 00:24:29,720
在WMAP数据中包含的信息
was that the information contained in the WMAP data

470
00:24:29,720 --> 00:24:32,790
并没有充分的
was, in itself, not sufficient

471
00:24:32,790 --> 00:24:36,960
证实或否定膨胀现象
to prove or refute inflation.

472
00:24:36,960 --> 00:24:39,760
弗里曼：他不是一个人在战斗
(Freeman) He wasn't alone.

473
00:24:39,760 --> 00:24:43,200
穿越非洲 另一个勇敢的科学家
Across the Atlantic, another intrepid scientist labored

474
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:47,570
不辞辛苦 致力于揭开宇宙创世后的真相
to uncover the truth behind what happened before the beginning.

475
00:24:47,570 --> 00:24:48,770
Paul Steinhardt
Paul Steinhardt

476
00:24:48,770 --> 00:24:51,840
他是普林斯顿大学物理系教授
is the Albert Einstein Professor of Physics

477
00:24:51,840 --> 00:24:53,570
另一个爱因斯坦
at Princeton University.

478
00:24:53,570 --> 00:24:55,340
作为一个年轻人
As a young man,

479
00:24:55,340 --> 00:24:59,280
Paul受月球登陆的激励 献身科研
Paul was inspired to study science by the moon landings.

480
00:24:59,280 --> 00:25:01,750
我们在这个年代选择重返月球
We choose to go to the moon in this decade

481
00:25:01,750 --> 00:25:03,150
并完成其他的工作
and do the other things,

482
00:25:03,150 --> 00:25:07,290
并不是因为工作容易 而是因为工作困难
not because they are easy, but because they are hard.

483
00:25:07,290 --> 00:25:09,290
[ Applause ]
[ Applause ]

484
00:25:11,390 --> 00:25:14,960
弗里曼：1999年, 这两个人联合起来
(Freeman) In 1999, the two men combined forces

485
00:25:14,960 --> 00:25:17,700
看看能否利用宇宙创世的 膨胀模型解决
to see if they could answer some of their problems

486
00:25:17,700 --> 00:25:20,970
一些难题
with the inflationary model of what happened at the beginning.

487
00:25:20,970 --> 00:25:23,370
膨胀理论取得了一些 不一般的成功
Inflation had some extraordinary successes,

488
00:25:23,370 --> 00:25:26,170
所以与膨胀理论竞争 是一场艰苦的赛事
so it's tough competition to compete with inflation.

489
00:25:26,170 --> 00:25:29,170
我们尝试过 然后又丢进废纸篓的主意
So I will not tell you all the ideas that were attempted

490
00:25:29,180 --> 00:25:30,840
那可是天上星，数不清啊
and dumped in the wastebasket.

491
00:25:30,840 --> 00:25:32,750
我们有类似的目标
We have similar objectives,

492
00:25:32,750 --> 00:25:35,980
那就是撼动"反动权威"
which is to shake the field up once in a while

493
00:25:35,980 --> 00:25:40,250
搞出些醒目、原创和特别的东西
and come up with something bold and original and different

494
00:25:40,250 --> 00:25:43,420
改进现状
and to improve on the status quo.

495
00:25:43,420 --> 00:25:46,160
Steinhardt博士：我和 Neil Turok一起组织了一个研讨会
(Dr. Steinhardt) I organized a conference with Neil Turok.

496
00:25:46,160 --> 00:25:48,560
我们对弦理论有共同兴趣
We had a common interest in string theory,

497
00:25:48,560 --> 00:25:51,000
这个理论那时才出现不久
which were just coming out at that time,

498
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:54,300
他们也许会给宇宙学研究 带来新的想法
whether they might stimulate some new ideas in cosmology.

499
00:25:54,300 --> 00:25:58,140
弗里曼：弦理论在过去 35年得到发展
(Freeman) String theory was developed in the last 35 years

500
00:25:58,140 --> 00:26:00,940
该理论试图用单一理论
as an attempt to devise a single theory

501
00:26:00,940 --> 00:26:03,680
解释宇宙中的万物
explaining everything in the Universe.

502
00:26:03,680 --> 00:26:08,410
在弦理论中，所有的东西都是 由很短的，振荡的弦组成
In it, everything is made of minute, vibrating strings.

503
00:26:08,420 --> 00:26:11,080
但是对弦理论使用的数学来讲
But for the mathematics of string theory to work,

504
00:26:11,080 --> 00:26:12,420
空间的维度必须超过3个
there have to be

505
00:26:12,420 --> 00:26:14,890
more than the three dimensions of space that we see.
more than the three dimensions of space that we see.

506
00:26:14,890 --> 00:26:18,690
实际上，包括时间在内，有10维
Rather, there are 10 dimensions, plus time.

507
00:26:18,690 --> 00:26:22,730
时空是弹性的，物质的 像是膜状物
Space-time is a flexible substance, like a membrane,

508
00:26:22,730 --> 00:26:25,030
能够拉伸和收缩
and it can stretch and shrink.

509
00:26:25,030 --> 00:26:27,300
我们知道这些东西可以移动
So, we knew these things could move,

510
00:26:27,300 --> 00:26:31,500
但是没有人真正的研究过 这个过程的动态变化
but nobody had really studied the dynamics of that process.

511
00:26:31,500 --> 00:26:35,370
我们请来了专家， 比如Burt Ovrut
So we brought in experts, like Burt Ovrut,

512
00:26:35,380 --> 00:26:39,480
他是对基于弦理论的 粒子物理模型
who is one of the most proficient developers

513
00:26:39,480 --> 00:26:42,710
最精通的研究者之一
of particle-physics models based on string theory.

514
00:26:42,720 --> 00:26:45,280
Steinhardt博士：他各我们做了 一系列精彩的讲座
(Dr. Steinhardt) And he gave a beautiful series of lectures

515
00:26:45,290 --> 00:26:46,520
向我们描述了这样一个学说
in which he described to us

516
00:26:46,520 --> 00:26:48,990
我们的三维世界
this idea of our three-dimensional world

517
00:26:48,990 --> 00:26:50,820
是嵌入在一个膜世界的
being embedded in a brane world

518
00:26:50,820 --> 00:26:53,760
若干膜世界沿着一个 额外的空间维度分布
separated by a small gap from another brane world

519
00:26:53,760 --> 00:26:55,890
彼此之间存在很小的间隙
along an extra spatial dimension.

520
00:26:55,900 --> 00:26:59,230
Turok博士：我们坐在那里 心中出现了同样的想法...
(Dr. Turok) And as we sat there, we both had the same thoughts...

521
00:26:59,230 --> 00:27:01,630
Steinhardt：那就是，如果你假设
(Dr. Steinhardt) ...Which is, if you imagine

522
00:27:01,630 --> 00:27:03,500
这是真正的宇宙结构
that this is really the structure of the Universe,

523
00:27:03,500 --> 00:27:05,240
就会有一个关于大爆炸的
there's a new possible interpretation

524
00:27:05,240 --> 00:27:06,370
新的解释
for what is the Big Bang.

525
00:27:06,370 --> 00:27:08,710
我们从未这样考虑过，你知道吗？
What have we not been facing up to, you know?

526
00:27:08,710 --> 00:27:10,510
屋里的大象是什么？
What is the elephant in the room?

527
00:27:10,510 --> 00:27:13,710
第一号问题就是奇点
And the number-one question was the singularity.

528
00:27:13,710 --> 00:27:17,280
我们从问题的两端接近Burt
We both sort of approached Burt from both ends...

529
00:27:17,280 --> 00:27:19,520
...在Burt的讲座结束时， 将他逼上绝路...
...And cornered Burt after his lecture...

530
00:27:19,520 --> 00:27:21,990
...我们补充完整了彼此的看法...
...And each of us finished the sentence of the other...

531
00:27:21,990 --> 00:27:23,260
...说，"你知道，呃
...And said, "you know, well,

532
00:27:23,260 --> 00:27:24,760
"如果这些东西碰撞会怎样？
"what about if these things collide?

533
00:27:24,760 --> 00:27:26,020
会发生啥事情？"
What would happen then?"

534
00:27:26,030 --> 00:27:28,460
"是否有可能，大爆炸不是开始
"And is it possible the Big Bang is not a beginning,

535
00:27:28,460 --> 00:27:29,460
而是一次 碰撞?"
but is a collision?"

536
00:27:30,330 --> 00:27:33,430
他的回答是，"也许"
And his response was, "maybe."

537
00:27:33,430 --> 00:27:36,670
弗里曼：会议很快结束了
(Freeman) The meeting soon broke up,

538
00:27:36,670 --> 00:27:39,510
但这三个人都被邀请参加
but the three men had all been invited

539
00:27:39,510 --> 00:27:42,310
当晚于伦敦上演的一出戏
to attend the same play in London that evening.

540
00:27:42,310 --> 00:27:45,010
Steinhardt：我们在火车站台碰面
(Dr. Steinhardt) We met at the train platform,

541
00:27:45,010 --> 00:27:50,880
我们开始认真设想更多的细节
and then we began to really imagine this idea in more detail

542
00:27:50,880 --> 00:27:53,950
如果大爆炸不是开始
about what it would mean if the Big Bang were not a beginning

543
00:27:53,950 --> 00:27:55,850
而是一场 碰撞
but the Big Bang were a collision.

544
00:27:55,860 --> 00:27:57,920
Turok博士：然后， 我们登上去伦敦的火车
(Dr. Turok) And then we had a train ride to London,

545
00:27:57,920 --> 00:28:00,460
我们用非常松散，非常非结构化 非常非数学化的方式
where we just brainstormed about this

546
00:28:00,460 --> 00:28:04,260
头脑风暴了一把
in a very loose and unstructured and unmathematical way.

547
00:28:04,260 --> 00:28:07,800
Steinhardt博士：我们问 自己这样的问题"我们能发现新东西
(Dr. Steinhardt) We asked ourselves the question, "could we invent something

548
00:28:07,800 --> 00:28:09,900
"与膨胀的说法不同
"which was different than the inflationary picture,

549
00:28:09,900 --> 00:28:11,870
与标准说法不同的东西吗？"
that was different than the standard picture?"

550
00:28:11,870 --> 00:28:13,870
Turok博士：我们有了某种 原始的想法
(Dr. Turok) We had some rough ideas how to do it,

551
00:28:13,870 --> 00:28:15,640
但一切还不太明朗
but it wasn't at all obvious.

552
00:28:15,640 --> 00:28:18,240
Steinhardt博士：火车前进，时光飞逝
(Dr. Steinhardt) Time was flying past us as the train was moving along.

553
00:28:18,240 --> 00:28:19,610
这是难得一遇的时机
It's one of those rare occasions

554
00:28:19,610 --> 00:28:21,180
你和别人讨论，
when you're having a conversation

555
00:28:21,180 --> 00:28:23,580
然后感到某种令人激动想法 渐渐成形
and you feel like a really exciting idea is emerging --

556
00:28:23,580 --> 00:28:24,650
第六感告诉我
sort of that sixth sense

557
00:28:24,650 --> 00:28:26,420
一些重要的事情正在发生
that something important is happening.

558
00:28:28,820 --> 00:28:32,190
和这些原始的想法一起出现 关于事物运行的规律
Coming up with this rough idea for how things might work

559
00:28:32,190 --> 00:28:33,760
当然，很激动人心
is, of course, exciting.

560
00:28:33,760 --> 00:28:36,300
但有这样一个想法
But in having an idea like that,

561
00:28:36,300 --> 00:28:39,500
并打算继续研究它
and then deciding to really pursue it,

562
00:28:39,500 --> 00:28:43,340
你等于把自己投入若干年的苦难
you are condemning yourself to years of misery,

563
00:28:43,340 --> 00:28:47,170
因为你必须给它充实血肉
because you now have to flesh this out.

564
00:28:48,070 --> 00:28:51,380
弗里曼：为了解决 这个神秘问题，Neil和Paul
(Freeman) And to solve this mystery, Neil and Paul

565
00:28:51,380 --> 00:28:54,510
会进行人类意识最困难的
would turn to one of the toughest mental challenges

566
00:28:54,510 --> 00:28:56,180
挑战之一
of the human mind --

567
00:28:56,180 --> 00:29:00,420
11维空间的难以置信的怪异世界
the incredibly strange world of 11-dimensional space...

568
00:29:00,420 --> 00:29:04,990
而且许多宇宙平行于我们的宇宙
And Universes parallel to our own.

569
00:29:07,630 --> 00:29:10,900
弗里曼：爱因斯坦 是一个令人敬畏的思想者
(Freeman) Albert Einstein was a formidable thinker.

570
00:29:12,270 --> 00:29:15,900
他关于相对性的理论 是开创性的进步
His theories of relativity were groundbreaking developments

571
00:29:15,900 --> 00:29:18,740
为一个世纪的宇宙学研究提供了启示
that triggered a century of cosmic insights.

572
00:29:18,740 --> 00:29:21,070
但更为基本和重要的是
But even more fundamental

573
00:29:21,070 --> 00:29:26,110
他意识到时间和空间是纠缠一体的
was his realization that time and space are intertwined.

574
00:29:26,110 --> 00:29:28,080
空间的三个维度
The three dimensions of space

575
00:29:28,080 --> 00:29:31,180
实际上是一个被称为"时空"的
are really part of a four-dimensional fabric

576
00:29:31,190 --> 00:29:33,850
四维构造的一部分
called "space-time."

577
00:29:33,850 --> 00:29:38,090
现在，在理论物理学 有一个新进展
But now there's a new movement in theoretical physics.

578
00:29:38,090 --> 00:29:41,960
称为"弦理论"
It's called "string theory."

579
00:29:41,960 --> 00:29:46,800
从弦理论中派生出了"M理论"
And out of string theory comes "m-theory."

580
00:29:46,800 --> 00:29:49,670
在M理论中，没有四维
In m-theory, there are not four,

581
00:29:49,670 --> 00:29:52,970
而是令人震惊的11维
but an astounding 11 dimensions --

582
00:29:52,970 --> 00:29:57,680
空间的10个维度加上时间维
10 dimensions of space plus one of time.

583
00:29:58,550 --> 00:30:01,610
啊，什么是M理论？ 啊，OK
Uh, what is m-theory? Uh, okay.

584
00:30:01,620 --> 00:30:05,850
嗯，啊，M理论是一个尝试，啊——
So, uh, m-theory is an attempt to, uh --

585
00:30:05,850 --> 00:30:07,390
让我再来一遍
let me start again.

586
00:30:07,390 --> 00:30:10,660
三维的无限世界拉伸——
Three-dimensional infinite worlds stretching off --

587
00:30:10,660 --> 00:30:12,160
啊，让我再来一遍
uh, let me start again.

588
00:30:12,160 --> 00:30:14,430
为什么一个人会考虑——
Why would one even think about --

589
00:30:14,430 --> 00:30:17,830
到底怎么做才能说完2句话 而不会让人觉得偶发疯？
how does one make that not sound crazy in two sentences?

590
00:30:17,830 --> 00:30:19,670
[笑]
[ Laughs ]

591
00:30:19,670 --> 00:30:23,300
哦，M理论是
So, m-theory is a...

592
00:30:23,300 --> 00:30:26,570
有希望成为，一统的理论
Promising, unified theory

593
00:30:26,570 --> 00:30:29,610
统一我们在自然界发现的
of all the fundamental forces and constituents

594
00:30:29,610 --> 00:30:31,340
所有的基本作用和组分
that we observe in nature.

595
00:30:31,350 --> 00:30:33,310
某种意义上，你可以这样描述它
In a sense, you could describe it

596
00:30:33,310 --> 00:30:35,720
作为整个20世纪，理论物理学
as the culmination of all the developments

597
00:30:35,720 --> 00:30:38,250
研究成果的总高潮
in theoretical physics over the 20th century.

598
00:30:38,250 --> 00:30:39,890
为了建立这个理论
In order to make this theory work,

599
00:30:39,890 --> 00:30:43,220
需要比通常的三维空间更多的维度
one needs to have more than the usual three spatial dimensions,

600
00:30:43,220 --> 00:30:44,790
所以在M理论中关键的一点是
so a key idea behind m-theory

601
00:30:44,790 --> 00:30:47,860
我们身处的空间
is that there are more than the three dimensions of space

602
00:30:47,860 --> 00:30:49,700
是超过三维的
that we experience.

603
00:30:49,700 --> 00:30:52,200
有隐藏的维度
There are hidden dimensions.

604
00:30:52,200 --> 00:30:54,200
实际上，有7个更多的维度
In fact, there are seven more,

605
00:30:54,200 --> 00:30:56,870
我们感觉不到它们的原因是
and the reason we're not aware of them

606
00:30:56,870 --> 00:31:00,510
它们是如此，如此微小 我们需要一个威力十分巨大的
is that they are so, so tiny that in order to see them,

607
00:31:00,510 --> 00:31:03,680
显微镜才能看到
you'd need an enormously powerful microscope

608
00:31:03,680 --> 00:31:06,310
一个前所未有的显微镜
far more powerful than any we have.

609
00:31:06,310 --> 00:31:10,180
我们的三维世界存在于一个表面
Our three-dimensional world lives in a surface

610
00:31:10,180 --> 00:31:14,390
表面嵌在空间中 该空间具有额外的空间维度
embedded in a space with an extra spatial dimension

611
00:31:14,390 --> 00:31:18,090
在这个维度上， 该表面与其它表面彼此分开
that separates it from another such surface.

612
00:31:18,090 --> 00:31:22,030
弗里曼：从这些额外维度中 出现了一种可能性
(Freeman) One possibility that springs from these extra dimensions

613
00:31:22,030 --> 00:31:24,630
也许另一个三维世界
is that this other three-dimensional world

614
00:31:24,630 --> 00:31:27,600
就藏在我们身边很近的地方
could be just a fraction of a centimeter from ours

615
00:31:27,600 --> 00:31:29,340
而我们却看不到
and yet hidden from our view.

616
00:31:29,340 --> 00:31:32,240
Steinhardt博士：这些表面 被叫做"膜"
(Dr. Steinhardt) These surfaces are called "branes,"

617
00:31:32,240 --> 00:31:33,610
就像是"细胞膜"
standing for "membrane,"

618
00:31:33,610 --> 00:31:36,640
是为了提醒我们 这些表面是弹性的
which is to remind us that these surfaces are elastic.

619
00:31:36,640 --> 00:31:39,450
它们能够拉伸，扭动，弯曲
They can stretch, they can wiggle, they can warp.

620
00:31:39,450 --> 00:31:42,180
它们能够沿额外维度移动
They can move along this extra dimension.

621
00:31:42,180 --> 00:31:44,580
我们发现的所有粒子
All of the particles we're made of

622
00:31:44,590 --> 00:31:47,190
实际上是由微小的膜卷成的
are actually curled-up little branes.

623
00:31:47,190 --> 00:31:50,160
我们身处其中的空间
And all the dimensions of space we travel in

624
00:31:50,160 --> 00:31:52,590
所有的维度都是由膜组成的
are comprised of branes themselves.

625
00:31:52,590 --> 00:31:54,960
宇宙中的万物
And so everything in the Universe

626
00:31:54,960 --> 00:31:57,960
都是由这些几何物体组成的
is composed of these geometrical objects.

627
00:31:57,970 --> 00:32:00,170
我不知道我是否能够重复 刚才所说的话
I don't know if I can repeat that again.

628
00:32:00,170 --> 00:32:01,170
[ 笑 ]
[ Laughs ]

629
00:32:01,170 --> 00:32:03,000
弗里曼：注意——
(Freeman) Caution --

630
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:07,140
你们刚进入了"膜世界"
you have entered a place called "brane world."

631
00:32:07,140 --> 00:32:10,540
Steinhardt博士：我们像苍蝇 撞上苍蝇纸一样，陷入了我们的膜世界
(Dr. Steinhardt) We're stuck like flies on fly paper to our brane world.

632
00:32:10,540 --> 00:32:13,010
我们只是找不到额外维——
We simply can't reach out into the extra dimension --

633
00:32:13,010 --> 00:32:16,750
即使其他的膜世界 仅在10的负30次方厘米之外
even 10 to the minus-30 centimeters --

634
00:32:16,750 --> 00:32:17,780
我们也无法触摸到
to touch the other brane world.

635
00:32:17,780 --> 00:32:20,720
弗里曼：这个膜世界理论 还很粗糙
(Freeman) It was rough this world of branes

636
00:32:20,720 --> 00:32:21,990
Paul和Neil
that Paul and Neil

637
00:32:21,990 --> 00:32:24,990
坎坷前行，试图建立一个有潜力的 激进的新理论
stumbled onto a potentially radical new theory

638
00:32:24,990 --> 00:32:27,590
新理论能够解释在宇宙起始之前 发生了什么事
of what happened before the beginning.

639
00:32:27,590 --> 00:32:30,060
这样，在这儿 我有一块布料
So, here I have a piece of material,

640
00:32:30,060 --> 00:32:32,900
看上去像是一个2维物体
and it looks like a two-dimensional object,

641
00:32:32,900 --> 00:32:35,400
一个维度向上
because one of the dimensions goes up

642
00:32:35,400 --> 00:32:37,100
另一个从一边到另一边
and one goes side to side.

643
00:32:37,100 --> 00:32:40,410
但是，如果我们凑近一些看
But if we look a little bit closer at this object,

644
00:32:40,410 --> 00:32:43,910
从这个方向看 你会发现，实际上
and look at it from the side, you'll see that actually

645
00:32:43,910 --> 00:32:46,210
有两块布料
there are two pieces of material,

646
00:32:46,210 --> 00:32:48,680
被一个微小的缝隙分开
separated by a tiny gap.

647
00:32:48,680 --> 00:32:50,780
你可以把这个缝隙
And you could think of this gap

648
00:32:50,780 --> 00:32:53,620
想象为空间的第四维
as being the fourth dimension of space.

649
00:32:53,620 --> 00:32:56,890
而这两个三维世界的碰撞——
And the collision of these two three-dimensional worlds --

650
00:32:56,890 --> 00:32:59,760
我们居住的世界和另一个——
the one we live in and another one --

651
00:32:59,760 --> 00:33:01,860
就是宇宙大爆炸
would have been the Big Bang.

652
00:33:01,860 --> 00:33:05,300
那会是一次碰撞， 而不再是生自虚无的变化
It would be a collision, instead of a springing from nothingness.

653
00:33:05,300 --> 00:33:07,700
所以，如果膜在此前和此后都存在
So, if the branes existed before and after,

654
00:33:07,700 --> 00:33:10,040
这意味着空间和时间 在此之前都存在
that means space and time existed before.

655
00:33:10,040 --> 00:33:11,600
这些膜也许有助于建立起
They could have helped set up

656
00:33:11,600 --> 00:33:14,010
我们今天所观察的宇宙的各种状态
the conditions we observe in the Universe today --

657
00:33:14,010 --> 00:33:16,010
他们碰撞，又各自分头前进
they collide, and they move apart again.

658
00:33:18,810 --> 00:33:20,880
大爆炸并不是起点
The Big Bang is not the beginning.

659
00:33:20,880 --> 00:33:22,450
这意味着我们有更多的时间
That means we have more time

660
00:33:22,450 --> 00:33:24,720
来解决所有的宇宙学难题
to solve all the cosmological problems

661
00:33:24,720 --> 00:33:26,920
膨胀理论就是被设计来 解决这些问题的
that inflation was designed to solve.

662
00:33:26,920 --> 00:33:29,660
我们开始想象 "我们能够用一些在大爆炸
So, we began to imagine, "could we replace that idea

663
00:33:29,660 --> 00:33:32,160
发生之前就存在的过程 代替那个理论吗？"
with something that occurred before The Bang?"

664
00:33:32,160 --> 00:33:34,460
当我们的火车前行
And as we were going along the train ride,

665
00:33:34,460 --> 00:33:36,730
我们开始想象许多可能性
we began to imagine lots of possibilities,

666
00:33:36,730 --> 00:33:37,900
然后，在火车到站的时候
so that by the end,

667
00:33:37,900 --> 00:33:40,170
看上去像是一个非常激动人心的
it seemed like a very exciting alternative

668
00:33:40,170 --> 00:33:42,670
与标准的大爆炸膨胀图景不同的理论
to the standard Big Bang inflationary picture.

669
00:33:44,800 --> 00:33:47,240
弗里曼：在接下来的18个月里
(Freeman) For the next 18 months,

670
00:33:47,240 --> 00:33:50,980
这三个人，以及另一个物理学家
Justin Khoury the three men and another physicist, Justin Khoury,

671
00:33:50,980 --> 00:33:54,010
狂热的工作，试图澄清和证明
worked feverishly to clarify and justify

672
00:33:54,010 --> 00:33:55,980
他们最初的灵感火花
their initial spark of creativity.

673
00:33:55,980 --> 00:33:58,980
Steinhardt博士：现在，我们 必须开始数学工作了
(Dr. Steinhardt) Now we had to make the mathematics work,

674
00:33:58,990 --> 00:34:02,050
有一个力试图把膜拉到一起
and this involved developing a lot of new physics

675
00:34:02,060 --> 00:34:05,690
为了解释在这个力的影响下
to explain the motion of branes moving along extra dimensions

676
00:34:05,690 --> 00:34:06,990
膜沿着额外维移动的过程
under the influence

677
00:34:06,990 --> 00:34:09,560
涉及许多物理学新进展
of a force which is trying to draw them together.

678
00:34:09,560 --> 00:34:11,600
这种数学之前并不存在
This mathematics didn't exist before.

679
00:34:13,430 --> 00:34:16,940
弗里曼：一个解释宇宙开始的新理论
(Freeman) A new theory of the Universe starts to come alive.

680
00:34:16,940 --> 00:34:19,540
Turok博士：我们脑中的画面是
(Dr. Turok) The picture we had in mind

681
00:34:19,540 --> 00:34:23,410
两个三维世界被无限拉伸
was two three-dimensional worlds stretching off to infinity

682
00:34:23,410 --> 00:34:26,510
但仍然彼此分开 中间存在一个小缝隙
but separated from each other by a tiny gap --

683
00:34:26,510 --> 00:34:28,510
空间第四维上的缝隙
a fourth dimension of space.

684
00:34:28,510 --> 00:34:30,880
这两个三维世界
The two three-dimensional worlds

685
00:34:30,880 --> 00:34:35,020
被一个非常非常微弱的力 拉在一起
are actually pulled together by a very, very weak force.

686
00:34:35,020 --> 00:34:38,320
这个力必须非常非常微弱
The force has to be very, very weak,

687
00:34:38,320 --> 00:34:41,690
否则大爆炸会发生的太快
otherwise the bang would occur too quickly.

688
00:34:41,690 --> 00:34:44,300
Steinhardt博士：我们知道 爆炸周期不能太短
(Dr. Steinhardt) We know that the cycles can't be too short,

689
00:34:44,300 --> 00:34:47,000
因为从上次大爆炸算起
because the Universe has already gone 14 billion years

690
00:34:47,000 --> 00:34:48,830
宇宙已经运行140亿年了
since the last bang.

691
00:34:48,840 --> 00:34:51,500
我们希望周期具有的 典型值是一万亿年
A trillion years is probably a good, you know, typical value

692
00:34:51,500 --> 00:34:53,670
这也许是一个比较合适的值
for what we expect the length of a cycle to be.

693
00:34:53,670 --> 00:34:55,970
Turok博士：当膜接近的时候
(Dr. Turok) As the branes approach,

694
00:34:55,980 --> 00:34:58,440
这个力越来越强
the force gets stronger and stronger.

695
00:34:58,440 --> 00:35:01,680
当它们碰撞，膜的动能
And when they collide, kinetic energy of the branes

696
00:35:01,680 --> 00:35:04,320
就转化为热辐射
is then converted into the hot radiation

697
00:35:04,320 --> 00:35:07,850
充满了碰撞的两个三维世界
that fills both three-dimensional worlds

698
00:35:07,850 --> 00:35:10,260
看上去就像大爆炸一样
and looks like the Big Bang.

699
00:35:10,260 --> 00:35:13,060
Steinhardt博士：所以当膜再次分开
(Dr. Steinhardt) So that when the branes move apart again,

700
00:35:13,060 --> 00:35:15,460
它们就充满了由碰撞产生的
they're now filled with the matter and radiation

701
00:35:15,460 --> 00:35:17,260
物质和辐射
that was created at the collision.

702
00:35:17,260 --> 00:35:21,500
这导致膜再次拉伸并变凉
This then causes the branes to begin to expand again and cool,

703
00:35:21,500 --> 00:35:24,640
创造了一个新的扩展和冷却周期
creating a new period of expansion, cooling,

704
00:35:24,640 --> 00:35:28,410
创造了新的原子、分子、恒星和星系
creation of new atoms, molecules, stars, and galaxies.

705
00:35:28,410 --> 00:35:31,740
我们现在有了对大爆炸的解释
We now had an explanation for the Big Bang.

706
00:35:31,740 --> 00:35:34,680
这通常是指"宇宙奇点"
This is normally referred to as "cosmic singularity" --

707
00:35:34,680 --> 00:35:37,180
物理学定律在此失效
some sort of breakdown in the laws of physics,

708
00:35:37,180 --> 00:35:40,220
在标准的大爆炸理论里 你简单的忽略了这些定律
which in the standard Big Bang theory, you simply ignore.

709
00:35:40,220 --> 00:35:41,490
但在这幅图景中
But in this picture,

710
00:35:41,490 --> 00:35:44,020
你为此提供了一个解释
you are actually providing an explanation for it.

711
00:35:44,020 --> 00:35:47,790
大爆炸，实际上，是两个膜世界 之间的碰撞
It was, in fact, the collision between these two brane worlds.

712
00:35:47,790 --> 00:35:51,000
这是关于宇宙奇点的一个理论
It was a theory of what was the cosmic singularity.

713
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:54,130
弗里曼：这是对时间问题， 宇宙最神秘问题之一的
(Freeman) It was a radical and elegant solution

714
00:35:54,130 --> 00:35:57,470
一个全新、优雅的解释
to one of the great cosmic mysteries of all time.

715
00:35:57,470 --> 00:35:59,470
根据Neil和Paul
According to Neil and Paul

716
00:35:59,470 --> 00:36:02,470
以及他们的同事Burt和Justin的说法
and their colleagues Burt and Justin,

717
00:36:02,480 --> 00:36:05,940
在时间之前总有时间
there was always a time before time.

718
00:36:08,480 --> 00:36:11,150
在将近2年的工作后
After almost two years of work, it was time

719
00:36:11,150 --> 00:36:14,350
是时候把这个新理论 展示给其他科学家了
to present this new theory to their fellow scientists.

720
00:36:14,350 --> 00:36:16,360
在芬兰的一个研讨会上
At a conference in Finland,

721
00:36:16,360 --> 00:36:19,490
这两个物理学家 介绍了他们的理论
the two physicists laid out their theory.

722
00:36:19,490 --> 00:36:21,460
反响冷淡
The reception was icy.

723
00:36:21,460 --> 00:36:24,500
批评者认为，我们只是简单的 假定和断言
The criticism was that we were simply assuming or asserting

724
00:36:24,500 --> 00:36:27,170
认为这些膜会是平的， 平行于起始状态，不会显示出来
the branes would be flat and parallel to begin with

725
00:36:27,170 --> 00:36:28,270
这是为什么呢~~
without showing why that should be the case.

726
00:36:28,270 --> 00:36:30,240
我们对这个想法非常激动
We'd been so excited about this idea,

727
00:36:30,240 --> 00:36:32,570
然而其他人只是被搞迷糊了
and yet everyone else was just poo-pooing it.

728
00:36:32,570 --> 00:36:35,680
公平的说，我认为 这个会议并不顺利
To be fair, I mean, the session did not go well for us.

729
00:36:37,040 --> 00:36:39,880
第二天造成，我俩情绪低沉
The next morning, we were both rather depressed,

730
00:36:39,880 --> 00:36:42,920
于是我们在Rovaniemi附近 沿河旅行
so we began to travel along the River near Rovaniemi

731
00:36:42,920 --> 00:36:44,350
开始讨论
and have this discussion

732
00:36:44,350 --> 00:36:46,820
"我们能用什么来代替这个主意？"
about "what could we replace this idea with?"

733
00:36:46,820 --> 00:36:48,220
所以，我们开始思考
So, we began to think

734
00:36:48,220 --> 00:36:50,960
思考某些还没被 包括进这个理论的东西
about something that wasn't yet included in the theory,

735
00:36:50,960 --> 00:36:52,890
那就是暗能量
which was the idea of dark energy.

736
00:36:55,490 --> 00:36:57,960
弗里曼：暗能量是近期一项
(Freeman) Dark energy is a recent

737
00:36:57,960 --> 00:37:01,370
引起了巨大震惊的天文发现
and totally surprising astronomical discovery --

738
00:37:01,370 --> 00:37:02,730
一种神秘的力量
a mysterious force

739
00:37:02,730 --> 00:37:06,270
它导致了宇宙加速膨胀
that's causing the Universe to expand even faster.

740
00:37:06,270 --> 00:37:09,870
最终，暗能量会使 宇宙的膨胀如此之剧烈
Eventually, the dark energy will expand the Universe so much

741
00:37:09,880 --> 00:37:12,880
以至于整个空间变为冷寂
that it will be nothing but cold and empty space.

742
00:37:12,880 --> 00:37:16,120
用M理论的语言 这可以被翻译成一个平膜
In the language of m-theory, that translates to a flat brane.

743
00:37:16,120 --> 00:37:21,520
暗物质相拉伸我们的三维世界
The dark-energy phase stretches out the three-dimensional worlds

744
00:37:21,520 --> 00:37:26,460
使它们变得非常平 非常空，非常平行
and makes them very flat and very empty and very parallel.

745
00:37:26,460 --> 00:37:29,700
当然，这立刻与另一个主意相通了
Of course, that immediately clicked with another idea.

746
00:37:29,700 --> 00:37:31,560
呃，我们现在利用某个东西
Well, we're using something now,

747
00:37:31,560 --> 00:37:33,930
但是我们是在 大爆炸之前 用到它
but we're using it before the bang.

748
00:37:33,930 --> 00:37:36,400
呃，也许，那时的暗能量之源
Well, maybe the source of dark energy then

749
00:37:36,400 --> 00:37:38,570
与现在的完全相同
was actually the same as the one now

750
00:37:38,570 --> 00:37:40,710
而宇宙以某种方式周期循环
and the Universe is cyclic somehow.

751
00:37:40,710 --> 00:37:42,880
Turok博士：这样，也许可以 有一次大爆炸
(Dr. Turok) So, you could have a bang

752
00:37:42,880 --> 00:37:46,480
接下来是宇宙的一段普通时期
followed by a normal period of the Universe,

753
00:37:46,480 --> 00:37:48,280
就像我们现在身处的一样
like we live in today,

754
00:37:48,280 --> 00:37:51,620
在未来，会有另一次大爆炸
followed by a second bang in our future,

755
00:37:51,620 --> 00:37:54,390
再一次，如此往复
followed by another bang, and so on.

756
00:37:54,390 --> 00:37:57,620
在之前，也存在 大爆炸、大爆炸、大爆炸
There are bangs and bangs and bangs forever.

757
00:37:57,620 --> 00:38:00,490
弗里曼：他们的理论仍不完备
(Freeman) Their theory was now complete.

758
00:38:00,490 --> 00:38:04,460
两个膜互相靠近 互相注入能量
Two branes come together, inject one another with energy,

759
00:38:04,460 --> 00:38:07,800
而暗能量花了万亿年的时间
then dark energy takes a trillion years or so

760
00:38:07,800 --> 00:38:09,700
将能量散布开来
to spread that energy out.

761
00:38:09,700 --> 00:38:13,470
膜再次变平 又彼此靠近
The branes flatten and then come together again.

762
00:38:13,470 --> 00:38:17,080
这个过程循环无尽
This cycle happens endlessly.

763
00:38:19,250 --> 00:38:22,210
Neil Turok和Paul Steinhardt 提出了一个关于大爆炸的
Neil Turok and Paul Steinhardt had come up with

764
00:38:22,220 --> 00:38:25,180
里程碑式的非传统理论
a remarkable alternative theory to the Big Bang

765
00:38:25,190 --> 00:38:29,320
敲响了通往创世之前的大门
and cracked the door onto what happened before the beginning.

766
00:38:29,320 --> 00:38:31,520
虽然模型各不相同
As different as the models are,

767
00:38:31,520 --> 00:38:34,390
但是它们都产生了完全一致的
they produce the same exact variations

768
00:38:34,390 --> 00:38:36,400
背景辐射
in the background radiation.

769
00:38:36,400 --> 00:38:39,930
两个理论都能解释WMAP图像
The same WMAP image fits both ideas.

770
00:38:39,930 --> 00:38:43,640
当WMAP的成果被宣布时
It's truly the case that when WMAP made its announcement,

771
00:38:43,640 --> 00:38:46,910
大多数人利用大爆炸和膨胀理论
the way most people interpreted that announcement was,

772
00:38:46,910 --> 00:38:48,340
解释这一成果
it's beautifully consistent

773
00:38:48,340 --> 00:38:50,480
这个理论的确非常美妙
with the Big Bang inflationary picture.

774
00:38:50,480 --> 00:38:53,210
对我们来说，周期模型 和膨胀理论
To us, it meant that the cyclic model was in the game

775
00:38:53,210 --> 00:38:54,510
是在同场竞技
as much as inflation was.

776
00:38:54,510 --> 00:38:57,520
弗里曼：但哪个理论是正确的呢？
(Freeman) But which theory is right?

777
00:38:57,520 --> 00:39:02,190
这个答案能够解释最高深的宇宙之谜
The answer to one of the biggest cosmic mysteries of all --

778
00:39:02,190 --> 00:39:05,490
在我们的时间之前，存在时间吗？
was there a time before our time? --

779
00:39:05,490 --> 00:39:11,060
在我们地球，我们的头上 一百万英里的地方盘旋
could be circling the Earth a million miles over our heads.

780
00:39:16,580 --> 00:39:18,990
弗里曼：在宇宙创世前发生了什么？
(Freeman) What happened before the beginning?

781
00:39:18,990 --> 00:39:21,190
问题摆在那儿 各路人马却都疲惫不堪
The question is posed. Sides are drawn.

782
00:39:21,190 --> 00:39:24,060
终场辩论正在准备之中
The closing arguments are being prepared.

783
00:39:24,060 --> 00:39:26,190
答案会是"啥也没有"？
Is the answer "nothing"?

784
00:39:26,190 --> 00:39:30,960
大爆炸是突然和无法理解的
Did a Big Bang suddenly and inexplicably burst into life

785
00:39:30,960 --> 00:39:35,000
从没有时间、没有空间的地方 爆发形成？
from a time of no-when and a place of nowhere?

786
00:39:35,000 --> 00:39:36,400
还是在我们之前就存在一个宇宙
Or could we have bounced

787
00:39:36,400 --> 00:39:38,740
我们只不过听到了它收缩时
from the contraction of another Universe

788
00:39:38,740 --> 00:39:40,870
发出的回声？
that existed before ours?

789
00:39:40,870 --> 00:39:44,540
哦 我们生活在平行宇宙的旁边吗？
Or are we living a trillionth of a trillionth

790
00:39:44,540 --> 00:39:48,780
它距离我们只有一个原子直径的 万亿分之一
of the width of an atom away from a parallel Universe,

791
00:39:48,780 --> 00:39:50,720
而每过一万亿年
and every trillion years,

792
00:39:50,720 --> 00:39:54,090
这些平行宇宙彼此碰撞
these parallel worlds bump into one another

793
00:39:54,090 --> 00:39:58,860
充满了巨大的能量和物质
and fill each other up with huge amounts of energy and matter?

794
00:40:01,760 --> 00:40:04,700
Martin Bojowald教授的活跃宇宙理论
Professor Martin Bojowald's bouncing Universe

795
00:40:04,700 --> 00:40:06,470
还在修改完善之中
is still a work in progress,

796
00:40:06,470 --> 00:40:10,740
但对宇宙周期论和 大爆炸膨胀理论的支持者而言
but for proponents of the cyclic and the Big Bang inflation model,

797
00:40:10,740 --> 00:40:13,770
针对宇宙何时和怎样开始 这一问题的答案
the answer to how and when the Universe started

798
00:40:13,770 --> 00:40:18,880
也许正在穿过时空 向我们飞来
may be moving toward us across time and space

799
00:40:18,880 --> 00:40:22,080
如同宇宙海洋中的微小波纹
like tiny ripples in the cosmic ocean...

800
00:40:23,150 --> 00:40:25,620
...引力波
...Gravitational waves.

801
00:40:25,620 --> 00:40:30,450
Turok：引力波很像是声波
(Dr. Turok) Gravitational wave is pretty much like a sound wave.

802
00:40:30,460 --> 00:40:31,790
[号角轰鸣]
[ Horn blares ]

803
00:40:31,790 --> 00:40:33,860
我们习惯了声波传播
We're used to a sound wave

804
00:40:33,860 --> 00:40:36,690
比如在我对你说话时 声波从我这儿传播到你那儿
traveling from me to you as I speak,

805
00:40:36,690 --> 00:40:41,930
声波是通过压缩和伸展 我们之间的空气传播的
as a compression and expansion of the air between us.

806
00:40:41,930 --> 00:40:45,800
在声波从我这儿传播到 你那儿的过程中
And so the molecules get more densely packed and further apart

807
00:40:45,800 --> 00:40:48,070
空气分子的密度时大时小
as the wave moves from me to you.

808
00:40:49,070 --> 00:40:51,110
弗里曼：引力波并不造成空气的涟漪
(Freeman) But gravitational waves ripple

809
00:40:51,110 --> 00:40:54,750
而是空间本身
not air molecules, but space itself, which means

810
00:40:54,750 --> 00:40:58,680
这就意味着他们会造成 一束光的伸展或压缩
that they can stretch out or compress a beam of light

811
00:40:58,680 --> 00:41:01,950
并导致光的色移
and cause a shift in its color.

812
00:41:01,950 --> 00:41:04,150
Turok博士：这样，如果空间扩展
(Dr. Turok) So, if space is expanded,

813
00:41:04,150 --> 00:41:05,920
我们会看到辐射出现
we'll see the radiation shifted

814
00:41:05,920 --> 00:41:08,260
红移现象，频率低，波长更长
to red frequencies, longer wavelengths.

815
00:41:08,260 --> 00:41:10,660
但是如果辐射是像我们飞来的
But if it's coming towards us, we'll see

816
00:41:10,660 --> 00:41:14,760
我们会看到蓝移现象
it's slightly bluer than it would otherwise have been.

817
00:41:14,760 --> 00:41:16,770
这样，通过仔细分析
And so, by carefully analyzing

818
00:41:16,770 --> 00:41:19,300
天空中辐射的模式
the pattern of radiation on the sky,

819
00:41:19,300 --> 00:41:23,510
我们可以，实际上，推断 引力波是否
we can, in fact, infer if there are gravitational waves

820
00:41:23,510 --> 00:41:26,540
经过这部分宇宙传播
traveling through our part of the Universe.

821
00:41:31,750 --> 00:41:33,820
弗里曼：火箭技术的发展
(Freeman) And rocket technology

822
00:41:33,820 --> 00:41:36,890
使科学家能够在太空中
will get the scientists far enough up into space

823
00:41:36,890 --> 00:41:39,190
观察这些引力波
to espy these gravitational waves.

824
00:41:42,160 --> 00:41:44,060
Spergel博士：普朗克卫星
(Dr. Spergel) The Planck satellite

825
00:41:44,060 --> 00:41:45,530
WMAP的继任者
is the successor to WMAP.

826
00:41:45,530 --> 00:41:48,600
它能够以2倍的分辨率和 10倍的灵敏度
It will be measuring the sky with about twice the resolution

827
00:41:48,600 --> 00:41:50,600
扫描天空
and about 10 times the sensitivity.

828
00:41:50,600 --> 00:41:53,040
普朗克卫星使我们第一次拥有了
The Planck satellite is really the first device we have

829
00:41:53,040 --> 00:41:54,870
也许能够找到"引力波"的
which seems to have a strong capability

830
00:41:54,870 --> 00:41:58,070
强大能力
of maybe finding"these gravity waves.

831
00:41:59,780 --> 00:42:02,780
如果我们走运
And if we're lucky, that'll tell us what happened

832
00:42:02,780 --> 00:42:05,350
它还会告诉我们，大爆炸之后 第一时刻发生了什么
during the first moments of the Big Bang,

833
00:42:05,350 --> 00:42:06,680
甚至更早时候的情形
or maybe even before.

834
00:42:10,320 --> 00:42:13,960
弗里曼：对大爆炸膨胀模型的 支持者来说
(Freeman) For proponents of The Big Bang inflation model,

835
00:42:13,960 --> 00:42:16,190
找到显著的引力波
finding significant gravitational waves

836
00:42:16,190 --> 00:42:18,230
也许是证明
would be the final step in proving

837
00:42:18,230 --> 00:42:21,060
存在一场无时无地爆发的大爆炸和
that there was a giant expansion of whooshing energy

838
00:42:21,060 --> 00:42:24,200
能量扩散的最后一步
from a place of nowhere and no-when.

839
00:42:24,970 --> 00:42:27,710
但是Paul Steinhardt和Neil Turok
But Paul Steinhardt and Neil Turok

840
00:42:27,710 --> 00:42:31,280
也在翘首盼望普朗克卫星的结果
are also looking forward to the Planck satellite results.

841
00:42:31,280 --> 00:42:34,450
在他们关于早期宇宙的周期模型中
In their cyclic model of the beginning of the Universe,

842
00:42:34,450 --> 00:42:36,010
两个膜彼此靠近
two branes coming together

843
00:42:36,010 --> 00:42:38,380
会是一个温柔的多的碰撞
would be a much less intense collision,

844
00:42:38,380 --> 00:42:40,020
他们成功的机会在于
and the chances are

845
00:42:40,020 --> 00:42:44,220
引力波也许基本不存在
that gravitational waves would be almost nonexistent.

846
00:42:44,220 --> 00:42:46,360
如果我们通过普朗克卫星
If we observe these gravitational waves

847
00:42:46,360 --> 00:42:47,630
观察到引力波
in the Planck satellite,

848
00:42:47,630 --> 00:42:49,830
这会是对膨胀理论的支持
that will support the inflationary theory

849
00:42:49,830 --> 00:42:51,430
而宣告周期模型的出局
and rule out the cyclic picture.

850
00:42:51,430 --> 00:42:53,500
相反，如果我们不能观察到引力波
And conversely, if we don't see them,

851
00:42:53,500 --> 00:42:55,970
则会强劲的支持周期模型
that would strongly support the cyclic picture.

852
00:42:55,970 --> 00:42:58,140
弗里曼：但是无论哪种理论
(Freeman) But no matter which description

853
00:42:58,140 --> 00:43:01,240
对早期宇宙描述更加精确
of the beginning of the Universe appears to be more accurate,

854
00:43:01,240 --> 00:43:03,570
真正的赢家都会是
the true winner will be

855
00:43:03,580 --> 00:43:07,110
我们人类的科学能力
our own scientific understanding.

856
00:43:07,110 --> 00:43:09,080
是的，对我来说，人类对抗自然
Yeah, to me, it's man against nature.

857
00:43:09,080 --> 00:43:11,350
我们努力揭示大自然的秘密
We're trying to figure out nature's secrets.

858
00:43:11,350 --> 00:43:13,420
如果我们走运 我们会得到惊喜的
If we're lucky, we'll be surprised.

859
00:43:15,620 --> 00:43:18,990
弗里曼：这些微小 几乎无法探测的波
(Freeman) These tiny, almost undetectable waves

860
00:43:18,990 --> 00:43:21,190
会给未来的宇宙学方向
will have a tsunami-like effect

861
00:43:21,190 --> 00:43:23,990
带来海啸般的影响
on the future direction of cosmology.

862
00:43:24,000 --> 00:43:27,700
替代那些无中生有
Instead of appearing from nowhere and no-when

863
00:43:27,700 --> 00:43:30,940
和来自人类幻觉的想法
and rising from stardust to humankind,

864
00:43:30,940 --> 00:43:34,410
我们可以考虑这些让人 惊讶的假定
we may have to consider the mind-boggling premise

865
00:43:34,410 --> 00:43:37,010
那就是我们只是
that we are just the latest version

866
00:43:37,010 --> 00:43:39,580
一系列无尽的宇宙中 最新的版本
of an endless series of Universes.

867
00:43:39,580 --> 00:43:43,880
我们仍然无法确定 在宇宙创世之前的情况
We still might not know what happened before the beginning...

868
00:43:43,880 --> 00:43:46,880
但我们会明了的
But we would know that something did.

869
00:43:46,890 --> 00:43:51,590
最终的答案也许近在手边
The final answer may be close at hand.

870
00:43:51,600 --> 00:43:55,600
-- 感谢观赏 --

